{
  "qualified": false,
  "scope": "Curved windowed observed-sea snapshot with exact local P1 hull clipping and current source/HOS BVP. No surface evolution, time pressure or coupled sixDOF trajectory.",
  "decision": "Keep experimental. Nonplanar geometry/BVP dataflow works on two supported inputs; independent field errors and P1/Fourier mismatch prevent qualification.",
  "findings": [
    "P1 exact six-mode self closure is about1e-13, but Fourier/P1 geometry differs. Canonical contact max error43.7->6.19mm and symmetric mask difference about0.119->0.0223m2 under local roof refinement.",
    "Independently refined Fourier hidden-area/pitch quadrature oscillates. Area/pitch closure is not certified or fully resolved; zero ambiguous midpoint samples do not bound missed cut cells.",
    "A one-ulp grid-center error created exact microedges and failed centroid fans. A second supported box exposed a thin-solid QHull diagnostic failure. Keep both failures.",
    "Final path constructs integer-indexed local axes and clips in a static CG-centered XY frame, with explicit local/world ownership and +k?origin wave-phase shift. No jitter, weld, vertex deletion or validator relaxation. This is not general sliver robustness.",
    "Canonical final-frame BVP force functionals reproduce the earlier world-frame successes within3.61e-12 SI. Both supported boats run unchanged from inputs; box field errors remain large, so it is an input/architecture control only.",
    "Canonical coarse/fine-roof184/216 P0 controls give about45%vertical/23%transverse known-field errors. Body refinement216->864 reduces physical-fill norms to17.8%/11.9%; water-grid129->257 alone changes them little.",
    "Coarse P1 roof with736 body panels fails the Fourier-centroid depth guard at?0.56mm. This failure is retained; no cutoff/sliver or target relocation was added. Independent finer-roof864 case stays5.58mm submerged.",
    "At N257/body216, HOSorder4->6 barely changes manufactured error norms and rigid coefficients; this does not establish fieldwise parity or global convergence.",
    "Known full auxiliary trace and physical exterior total-fill remain independent verification inputs to the same solver. Extension sensitivity is still material and not qualified.",
    "Exact analytical panel-pressure moments distinguish centroid quadrature, field error, and physical-domain change between roofs.",
    "Four independent query/frame tests pass; adversarial source reviews approve geometry, flux signs, coordinate/wave ownership and BVP scope."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Current BVP uses actual Fourier graph with an approximate P1 wet cut; body-air strips and unresolved waterline geometry remain explicit.",
    "No identical-curved-domain external physical load reference. Rigid coefficients alone are not validation.",
    "Source fixture stays fixed and strictly within the full physical solid; point-pair forcing is demanding and does not dictate production mesh counts.",
    "No nonlinear trajectory speed or60s motion-accuracy qualification. Component timings include verification work and are not time-domain throughput.",
    "P1 constructor retains its diagnostic plane/time/bed budgets. No volume fluid mesh is sent to the new BVP.",
    "Future moving stencils must hold a translated frame fixed or own frame-transport terms; this stage is static."
  ],
